    {
      "is_best": true,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>It should be possible to find the <strong>Edit </strong>function under the menu with the three dots at the top right of your post.</p><p>Regards<br/>/Peter</p></div>"
    },
    {
      "is_best": false,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Hello ​<user-mention data-id=\"38474\">@Jack3</user-mention>, <br/><br/>The edit option is open for 60min after the post has been created. After that, this option is no longer available. <br/><br/>Kind regards,<br/>Lina</p></div>"
    },
    {
      "is_best": false,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Why 60 minutes? Why not 60 days? Is it temporary or permanent? I frequently edit my posts with improved formatting, spelling/grammar, and extra context. In fact I think I edit most of my posts several times.</p></div>"
    },
    {
      "is_best": false,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>As the others have said, you should be able to edit your own post - via the menu at top-right of the post:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/ddd8a880-1ae9-43e9-a124-e96acb1cd0e1.png\"/></figure><p> </p><p>But you can no longer edit the title:</p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/feedback-forum-118/can-t-edit-post-title-165974\"></oembed><p> </p></div>"
    },
    {
      "is_best": false,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>​<user-mention data-id=\"38474\">@Jack3</user-mention> , If you need to edit content past 60min, you can Report the message and share the changes that needs to be done. <br/><br/>Regards,<br/>Lina</p></div>"
    },
    {
      "is_best": false,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>See also:</p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/feedback-forum-118/allow-to-edit-posts-166661\"></oembed><p> </p></div>"
    }
  ]
